2-5iz &= 3
\end{align*}

Next, we can add $5iz$ to both sides to isolate the term with $z$:

\begin{align*}
2-5iz &= 3 \\
2-5iz + 5iz &= 3 + 5iz \\
2 &= 3 + 5iz
\end{align*}

Now, we can subtract $3$ from both sides to isolate the term with $z$:

\begin{align*}
2 &= 3 + 5iz \\
2 - 3 &= 3 + 5iz - 3 \\
-1 &= 5iz
\end{align*}

Finally, we can divide both sides by $5i$ to solve for $z$:

\begin{align*}
-1 &= 5iz \\
\frac{-1}{5i} &= \frac{5iz}{5i} \\
